Subject: [PATCH 02615/11362] [outer-loop] correct config direction: a GENERAL
 rule-INDUCER, not per-game rules (operator correction)

Operator corrected the Stage 1+2 kill conclusion: 're-scope to per-game rules' is the GameAdapter
anti-pattern (less general). The right target is a general config-rule solver that INTROSPECTS a new
game and DERIVES its win-rule from a library of config-rule TYPES abstracted from previously-seen
config games -- meta-learning the rule-space, the SAME verifier-grounded-induction thesis as the rest
of the project. Reconciliation: Stage 2 killed config-MATCH and PROVED the wins are relational/rule-
based -- which MOTIVATES rule-induction, it does not refute it; I never tested rule-induction. Appends
the corrected architecture (introspect -> hypothesize rule-type from library -> VERIFY (Carnot) ->
solve, with the executor + inducer co-dependent), re-aims the gates, and lists the first experiments:
rule-type catalogue, an LLM rule-induction probe on a KNOWN-rule game (tr87), then verify-then-solve.
Stage 3 (rule induction) is the correct primary build, not pointless.

